# Prada RTW size options

Official Prada ready-to-wear PDP size pickers are the source of truth.

## Do

- Prefer PDP HTML `aria-label="Select size …"` via `pr_sizes.rtw_sizes` / `sizes_from_pdp_html`
- Use `availableSizesStore` / `availableSizes` for codes + online stock
- Keep short variants (`46S`, `48S`) as separate purchasable sizes when the PDP shows them
- When any `…S` size is offered, size charts must include Short guidance via
  `pr_size_charts._enrich_chart_with_short_sizes` (note + **Short (S) 사이즈** tab;
  body cm matches standard; length −5 cm per prada.com)
- Run `python3 scripts/verify-pr-rtw-sizes.py` and `python3 scripts/test_pr_sizes.py` after size changes
- After catalog writes, `patch-pr-rtw-short-size-charts.py` (also called from `build-pr-catalog`)

## Do not

- Never merge Algolia `SizeGroupStore` letter labels (`S`/`M`/`L`/`XL`) into the variant list when numeric IT/waist sizes exist — those letters are conversion-chart labels, not PDP picker SKUs
- Never ship a product with both letter sizes and numeric sizes in `sizes` / `variants` (e.g. `S, M, L, 48, 50`)
- Never ship a product that sells `46S`/`48S` without Short length info in `sizeChart`

## Guards already in place

- `pr_sizes.assert_no_mixed_rtw_sizes` — scrape refresh / catalog build hard-fail
- `scripts/verify-pr-rtw-sizes.py` — raw + catalog check
- `scripts/test_pr_sizes.py` — regression for the GEB310-style Algolia mix
- `scripts/patch-pr-rtw-short-size-charts.py` — Short tab/note on RTW charts
